<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>IMPOSTER SCAMS</strong>&nbsp;often begin with a call, text message, email or direct message through social media.&nbsp;The scams may vary, but most work the same way &ndash; a scammer pretends to be someone you trust to convince you to send them money or share personal information. They often use fear tactics and pressure you to respond quickly. <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" href="https://mercantilebk.com/resource-library/id-theft-security/imposter-scams" target="_blank">Continue Reading</a></p>
